e":277,"line":39},{"w":"hand","s":277,"e":277.56,"line":39},{"w":"shook","s":277.56,"e":278,"line":39},{"w":"One","s":278,"e":278.98,"line":39},{"w":"rifle","s":278.98,"e":279.42,"line":39},{"w":"dropped","s":279.42,"e":279.92,"line":39},{"w":"One","s":279.92,"e":280,"line":39},{"w":"One","s":279.92,"e":280.98,"line":40},{"w":"brave","s":280.98,"e":281.42,"line":40},{"w":"no","s":281.42,"e":281.96,"line":40},{"w":"And","s":281.96,"e":283.24,"line":40},{"w":"the","s":283.24,"e":283.64,"line":40},{"w":"battle","s":283.64,"e":284.62,"line":40},{"w":"stopped","s":284.62,"e":285.74,"line":40}],"lines":[{"s":9.12,"e":17.7,"text":"One hand shook, one rifle fell One soul stepped from a living hell"},{"s":17.62,"e":28.82,"text":"No boom in sky, no blaze in fuse Just one brave soldier who refused"},{"s":42.5,"e":48.94,"text":"Yeah, boots in the mud, blood on the boots Truth getting buried beneath the salutes"},{"s":50.04,"e":58.12,"text":"Yeah, young boys boxed in the battles in blues Born with a future, then forced to choose"},{"s":58.5,"e":64.8,"text":"Yeah, cocomands crack through a crooked connection March towards the smoke in the enemy's direction"},{"s":65.66,"e":73.76,"text":"But across that field, through the ash and aggression He caught one kid's eyes and caught his reflection"},{"s":74.36,"e":79.06,"text":"Yeah, same mama praying, face in the floor Same father waiting beside the front door"},{"s":78.98,"e":88.82,"text":"Same baby sister saying, come home from the war Same dreams that deserve to be something more"},{"s":89.92,"e":95.24,"text":"Same shaking hands, same sweat, same stress Same hard hammering, heart in his chest"},{"s":95.16,"e":99.34,"text":"So we lower the barrel, let bravery bloom I won't turn somebody's baby to new"},{"s":99.26,"e":103.26,"text":"Commander can't crash it, do what you're told But courage gets clearer when conscience gets dulled"},{"s":103.18,"e":108.14,"text":"He dropped that rifle, let mercy take hold I'd rather save souls than surrender my soul"},{"s":108.06,"e":117,"text":"One gun down, then two touched ground Then ten and ten thousand, no thunder, no sound"},{"s":116.92,"e":123.74,"text":"The last soldier refused to fight Dropped all the darkness, defended the light"},{"s":123.66,"e":131.98,"text":"One little note multiplied overnight Till millions stood still and remembered what's right"},{"s":131.9,"e":140,"text":"No, no more mothers with midnight notes No more children paying powerful dues"},{"s":140.52,"e":149.3,"text":"Peace began when somebody chose You can order the war, but my soul can't refuse"},{"s":149.22,"e":153.04,"text":"Other side staring through smoke in surprise One soldier still with his hands to the skies"},{"s":152.96,"e":157.04,"text":"And another step forward, then five, then fifty Fear got fragile when mercy got risky"},{"s":156.96,"e":160.94,"text":"Steel started stacking in shimmering rows Rifles lay resting where red rivers flow"},{"s":160.86,"e":165.04,"text":"No victory screaming, no vengeance to prove Just people with pulses refusing to lose"},{"s":164.96,"e":168.86,"text":"Lose that love, lose that light Lose one more brother to somebody's fight"},{"s":168.78,"e":172.84,"text":"Can't make me hate who I never have met Can't make his children inherit our debt"},{"s":172.84,"e":176.88,"text":"Presidents pleading, generals grieving For power that vanished when people stopped believing"},{"s":176.8,"e":181.34,"text":"Though this mean nothing when millions decide That courage is choosing to keep someone alive"},{"s":181.26,"e":185.22,"text":"East and west, every enemy raced Every enemy finally given a face"},{"s":185.14,"e":192.46,"text":"And history wrote what the powerful knew A war needs soldiers, and the soldiers withdrew"},{"s":192.94,"e":200.6,"text":"Maybe bravery isn't a bullet or blade Maybe strength is the life that you save"},{"s":200.8,"e":207.42,"text":"Maybe winning is walking away From hatred handed from yesterday"},{"s":208.68,"e":212.9,"text":"Maybe peace isn't passive or weak Maybe peace is the bravest we speak"},{"s":212.82,"e":222.84,"text":"Maybe one voice when honest and true Can give ten million permission to choose"},{"s":222.76,"e":226.8,"text":"One step, one stand One heart, one hand"},{"s":226.72,"e":230.18,"text":"One weapon down Then weapons worldwide"},{"s":236.34,"e":242.12,"text":"The last soldier refused to fight Then millions marched on"},{"s":242.2,"e":246.46,"text":"Mercy and light Every battlefield fell"},{"s":246.38,"e":249.66,"text":"Silent that night Nobody conquered"},{"s":249.58,"e":255.94,"text":"But everybody survived No more mothers with midnight news"},{"s":255.86,"e":263.8,"text":"No more children paying powerful dues Peace began when somebody chose"},{"s":263.72,"e":270.2,"text":"You can order the war But my soul can refuse"},{"s":275.84,"e":280,"text":"One hand shook One rifle dropped"},{"s":279.92,"e":285.74,"text":"One brave no And the battle stopped"}],"duration":292.2,"source":"whisper","generatedAt":"2026-06-01T00:00:00.000Z"}